      "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n## What does this PR do?\n\nThis PR preserves an explicit `temperature=0.0` when an RL request passes through `MegatronLocal`, while retaining `1.0` as the default when temperature is unspecified. The old truth-value fallback treated both `None` and floating-point zero as missing; the fix uses an explicit `None` check so only an omitted value receives the default.\n\n## Example failure scenario(s)\n\n**Scenario (explicit zero temperature)**\n\n- Request A sets `temperature=0.0` for greedy output.\n- The old code treats `0.0` as missing and sends `1.0`.\n- The model can sample instead of choosing the most likely token.\n- The fix preserves `0.0` and keeps the request greedy.\n\n## How was this bug discovered?\n\nWhile making RL inference comparisons deterministic, the setup requested `temperature=0.0` and inspected the keyword arguments forwarded by `MegatronLocal`. It observed `1.0`, although an explicit zero should have been forwarded unchanged. The detection oracle is the mocked client's exact received temperature for both relevant cases: an omitted temperature must become `1.0`, while an explicit `0.0` must remain `0.0`.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nLinked issue: N/A\n\n## Contribution process\n\n### Pre-checks\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests\n- [ ] I have added proper typing to my code [Typing guidelines](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html)\n- [ ] I have added relevant documentation\n- [ ] I have run the [autoformatter.sh](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/main/tools/autoformat.sh) on my PR\n\n## Validation\n\nExact signed tip: `abcdda5160de412644a7bf131bb2b93c7e6407f4`\n\n- DFW Slurm job `17582623`: passed at the exact signed tip\n  - omitted temperature defaults to `1.0`\n  - explicit `temperature=0.0` remains `0.0`\n  - 2 passed, 0 failed, and 0 skipped on each of 8 ranks\n- isort and Black passed on the changed-import test file.\n- Ruff and Python bytecode compilation passed on both changed Python files.\n- `git diff --check 3c04d2bd2255c9652a687c3d5a5b9636467696db...abcdda5160de412644a7bf131bb2b93c7e6407f4` passed.\n",
